From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:16:38 -0700
Subject: [M150] Don't hold a reference to the id attribute across UpdateId()

Original change's description:
> Don't hold a reference to the id attribute across UpdateId()
>
> Element::InsertedInto() took a reference into the element's attribute
> storage via GetIdAttribute() and passed it to UpdateId(). UpdateId()
> notifies id target observers, and those can update style and layout.
> For example, a focused <input list> whose datalist became usable
> rebuilds its shadow tree and calls RevealSelection(). If that update
> builds a <use> instance tree that clones the element, cloning
> serializes the element's dirty style attribute and appends it to the
> attribute storage. When that reallocates the storage, the reference
> dangles, and the remaining reads of the id in UpdateId() access freed
> memory.
>
> This CL copies the id into a local AtomicString before calling
> UpdateId(). RemovedFrom() passes the id to UpdateId() the same way, so
> it gets the same change. Recent fixes for similar bugs in
> ElementRuleCollector and HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink()
> used the same approach.
>
> Fixed: 567638392
